{
  "_doc": "ChEMBL 37 (mechanism.jsonl + molecule_max_phase4.jsonl + target.jsonl): the Drug and ProteinTarget nodes, the HAS_MECHANISM edge between them, the OF_ORGANISM edge that carries a target onto an NCBI Taxon — the one field in ChEMBL that touches a microbe, and what makes D8 partially answerable while MASI is pending — and IS_DRUG, which makes the Intervention nodes gutMDisorder mints from DrugBank ids reachable from a ChEMBL id. Drug is keyed on the PARENT molecule, so a salt form is the same drug: 1,626 mechanism rows name a salt and keying on molecule_chembl_id would split those drugs in half. The Intervention entry declares connections only — gutMDisorder owns that node's table, the way core.json owns Taxon's.",
  "_files": "Every table this fragment reads, declared once. A frame the build hands over by name; the preps fill it, nothing on disk backs it.",
